    "The italicized second 'thy' is no longer 'added': ἐξ ἀριστερῶν is anarthrous, so rule 51's anarthrous clause makes the supplied possessive a rule 7 helper on the substantival adjective it determines, matching this chapter's own treatment of γυναῖκα → 'his wife' at 10:2 under rule 24's habit. Rule 103 is scoped to supplied lexical content and names a pronoun as the contrast that folds.",
